---
import ArchitecturePage from '../../components/ArchitecturePage.astro';
import cadThinking from '../../data/architecture/cad-agent-thinking.json';

const visibleSignals = [
	'The user request and linked part identity',
	'Selected workflow mode and planning attempt',
	'Bounded feature, parameter, dependency, and fingerprint context',
	'The strict ToolPlan summary, registered operations, and impact review',
	'Typed preflight or validation diagnostics used for repair',
	'Public milestone events and the final changed or no-change outcome',
];

const protectedSignals = [
	'Hidden token-by-token model deliberation or private chain of thought',
	'Prompt text, complete source bodies, credentials, or storage access',
	'Unvalidated intermediate source or partial operation results',
];

const planningTools = [
	{ name: 'confirm_no_change', mode: 'Established edit', purpose: 'Prove with semantic IDs and current function-body fingerprints that accepted source already satisfies the request.' },
	{ name: 'write_initial_model', mode: 'Initial design only', purpose: 'Supply the complete AI-owned model body behind the system-owned runtime import.' },
	{ name: 'replace_parameter_field', mode: 'Established edit', purpose: 'Replace one existing annotated ModelParams field using its exact editable target and fingerprint.' },
	{ name: 'add_model_parameter', mode: 'Established edit', purpose: 'Add one new annotated ModelParams field with a default.' },
	{ name: 'delete_model_parameter', mode: 'Established edit', purpose: 'Delete one explicitly provenance-owned, unreferenced model parameter.' },
	{ name: 'update_cad_part_metadata', mode: 'Established edit', purpose: 'Replace the bounded role, parameters, dependencies, and search keys of an existing semantic feature.' },
	{ name: 'replace_cad_feature_body', mode: 'Established edit', purpose: 'Replace statements inside an existing public CAD feature selected by semantic ID.' },
	{ name: 'add_cad_feature', mode: 'Established edit', purpose: 'Add one new server-decorated public semantic CAD feature.' },
	{ name: 'delete_cad_feature', mode: 'Established edit', purpose: 'Delete one eligible existing semantic PART region.' },
	{ name: 'replace_function_body', mode: 'Established edit', purpose: 'Replace statements inside an existing private helper.' },
	{ name: 'add_private_helper', mode: 'Established edit', purpose: 'Add one new private synchronous helper function.' },
	{ name: 'delete_private_helper', mode: 'Established edit', purpose: 'Delete one explicitly provenance-owned, unreferenced private helper.' },
	{ name: 'replace_build_model_body', mode: 'Established edit', purpose: 'Replace only the statements inside build_model to update final assembly.' },
];
---

<ArchitecturePage
	title="CAD Agent Thinking Flow"
	summary="An auditable view of what the CAD agent considers and in what order: bounded context, structured planning, deterministic preflight, no-change or candidate branching, validation feedback, and proof-gated completion."
	section="Reasoning view"
	active="cad-thinking"
	document={cadThinking}
	fallback="Loading the CAD Agent thinking diagram…"
	showExampleNotice={false}
	diagramFirst={true}
	sidebarNote="Production reasoning view: observable inputs, decisions, registered tool plans, deterministic checks, repair feedback, and terminal outcomes."
>
	<h2>What “thinking” means here</h2>
	<p>This page visualizes the system’s inspectable decision process, not a private chain-of-thought transcript. Each numbered card is an implementation-backed stage. Select a card or connector to inspect its inputs, decisions, guarantees, failure behavior, and source evidence.</p>

	<h2>What operators can observe</h2>
	<ul>
		{visibleSignals.map((signal) => <li>{signal}</li>)}
	</ul>

	<h2>What the progress stream intentionally excludes</h2>
	<ul>
		{protectedSignals.map((signal) => <li>{signal}</li>)}
	</ul>

	<h2>Registered tools available to the planning model</h2>
	<p>OpenAI does not receive general Python, shell, database, or storage tools. It can only propose the following structured CAD operations inside a <code>ToolPlan</code>. The Python CAD Tool Worker treats every proposed operation as untrusted input and independently validates its mode, arguments, scope, ownership, source hash, and target fingerprints before execution.</p>
	<table>
		<thead>
			<tr>
				<th scope="col">Tool</th>
				<th scope="col">Available in</th>
				<th scope="col">Purpose</th>
			</tr>
		</thead>
		<tbody>
			{planningTools.map((tool) => (
				<tr>
					<th scope="row"><code>{tool.name}</code></th>
					<td>{tool.mode}</td>
					<td>{tool.purpose}</td>
				</tr>
			))}
		</tbody>
	</table>

	<h3>System actions that are not model tools</h3>
	<p>Context preparation, repair-context preparation, candidate validation, canonical commit, rollback, semantic reindexing, export queueing, storage access, database access, and public progress publication remain server- or worker-owned actions. The model can neither invoke them directly nor bypass their checks.</p>

	<h2>Reading the two terminal paths</h2>
	<p><strong>No change:</strong> when current source definitely satisfies the request, the plan uses one fingerprint-backed <code>confirm_no_change</code> operation. Python verifies that evidence and Nest completes without a candidate, validation, commit, post-edit reindex, or export.</p>
	<p><strong>Source change:</strong> registered operations pass both plan gates, execute transactionally in memory, produce one isolated candidate, and enter independent validation. A repairable failure loops back with typed diagnostics; only exact validation proof can reach canonical commit.</p>
</ArchitecturePage>
